//! Subcommand: `fusible body` — build the physical bodies of the project.
//!
//! A body is either authored in any CAD tool (`source:`, optionally produced by a
//! `build:` command) or generated by Fusible (`generate: enclosure`). For the
//! enclosure, Fusible computes the whole layout (outline, screw bosses, edge notches,
//! vents) from Circuit JSON, then hands a JSON spec to an embedded TypeScript generator
//! that runs the OpenCascade kernel (`occt-wasm`) under bun and writes the CAD files.

